Eve desktop 1.5.0
The Electron/TypeScript application is MIT licensed. The Python implementation
retains its original Apache-2.0 license and module/API identifiers for compatibility.
The shared skill library contains upstream reference instructions and resources.
Pinned source commits, per-skill licenses and copyright notices are retained in
skill-library/index.json and its content-addressed library.pack. Read a selected
LICENSE resource through skill_read_resource. Import and omission decisions are
recorded in skill-library/import-report.json. No upstream scripts run on installation.

The shared scientific catalog includes K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills at
commit 5f2bc0341354fd5590aef76a533ada1e1e5b4e62 (MIT). Upstream license files,
source paths and resource digests are retained per skill. Entries marked by the
upstream project as non-redistributable, including deepspot-m and rowan, are not
included. Their absence is intentional and is recorded in the import report.

The research workflow adapts the stage/evidence mechanisms of ResearAI/DeepScientist
(b36624417f0c6b8238ec02db37b94d6db2faa5b0, Apache-2.0) to Eve's existing RunService.
There is no second DeepScientist runner. No ClawsGO binaries or assets are shipped.

The bundled MinerU skill is sourced from opendatalab/MinerU
(b7f3dd0c5f6e6d66a298239ffd02b328b873918e). MinerU is licensed under
Apache-2.0 with additional terms; the complete upstream license is retained
inside the skill library as EVE-UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt. Eve identifies MinerU in
this notice and in the skill's source metadata wherever the skill is made
available through an online service.

Electron includes Chromium/Node.js with their separate third-party notices.
The scientific skill bundle retains the notices of Google LLC from
google-deepmind/science-skills (4de6786171f1479026da5d3a00f110703c8ba35e, v1.3.1).
Software is Apache-2.0; other materials are CC-BY-4.0. Each prepared skill
includes EVE-UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt, EVE-MATERIALS-LICENSE.txt and
EVE-DATA-SOURCE-TERMS.md. Individual databases retain their own terms.
Eve is not an official Google product.
Resolved Node runtime license texts are under third-party-licenses/.
The interactive visualization skill contains Archify v3.2.0
(tt-a1i/archify, 208acba8d412335185b2056fedf54b3405df43fb, MIT).
Its complete license, instructions and executable resources remain in the
verified shared library; EVE-UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt accompanies prepared files.
Python itself and its dependencies are not bundled; the managed dependency setup
uses an available interpreter. Original Python sources and LICENSE ship under
resources/legacy. Renderers and workers use the existing isolation boundaries;
subprocess isolation is not an operating-system security sandbox.

Additional scientific workflows retain Apache-2.0 notices from
anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins, revision 2574e29377c7173d0cecffef29a6ecbd7f8ccb5d.
Specialist scientific model skills retain the original notices from
NVIDIA-BioNeMo/bionemo-agent-toolkit, revision f9bb5bb3aacc881c89eb15e93fd119e91915eea8:
Apache-2.0 source code, CC-BY-4.0 materials, and separately declared BSD-3-Clause
workflow helpers. Complete upstream notices and source identities accompany
each prepared skill. Eve's runtime adaptation metadata is separate from the
unchanged original skill and script resources. Model weights and third-party
services are not bundled and remain subject to their own access and terms.
User-installed research packs with unspecified redistribution terms are kept
in the user's runtime/science-library and are not included in this distribution.
